		(uuid "74e4c996-26b8-4d83-b573-a2b6c71af929")
	)
	(text "Five fitted cells, carried forward with no value changed (AS_BUILT S2).\nDigital divider bottoms return to PGND. Both ADC divider bottoms, their\nfilter and clamp returns, J2.6 (the B16 cluster ground sense) and Pico\nAGND are ONE node, bonded at a single point (S4, delta D5, R06-REV-1).\nLayout must not create a second path to it. B16 must never become a\npower return - but the fitted opto LED returns on it, so as drawn it\ncarries 4.7-5.8 mA whenever the engine runs. See the ignition note, Q2\nand review finding R06-REV-2: that conflict is the electrical lead's.\nBoth ADC channels already carry 1k + 1uF + two 1N5819 - fitted, not new (D3 closed)."
		(at 845.82 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85ada91d-cd5d-4ce0-9767-531aaa697a29")
	)
	(text "Placeholders, and delta D4"
		(at 845.82 63.50 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "624c20d8-47a9-4fd2-b9d3-6f530e04115c")
	)
	(text "PLACEHOLDER (dashed, \"?\", NOT SELECTED) = a block LRA-06 captures but does\nnot resolve. X1-X5 are delta D4: normally-open, power-off-safe isolation\nupstream of a divider top. Five positions, one per branch, in two states\nafter the owner key-out measurement of October 29 (D-OFFSTATE-01):\n  REQUIRED  - B2 only, and on a back-feed path rather than only a drain.\n              Four readings in one configuration fix it with nothing\n              estimated: 4.669 V open-circuit, 4.140 V loaded at the\n              tap, 1.042 V at the 22k/33k junction, 0.883 V on the clamp\n              cathodes. B2 draws 140.8 uA. The divider is not the only\n              load: a clamp is forward-biased, so only 31.6 uA reaches\n              ground through the 33k and 109.2 uA is back-fed into the\n              Pico 3V3 rail while the board is off. One branch is 141%\n              of the whole 100 uA system parked budget and 17.6x the\n              8 uA allocated to all five together, and it partially\n              energizes a board meant to be dead. This is the one row\n              of the S6 off-state matrix established by measurement\n              rather than by nothing. Parked source 3,757 ohm.\n  UNDER REVIEW - B1 and C11 measure 0 V key out, and C14 and B11 were\n              already recorded dead. The parked-drain justification is\n              withdrawn for these four; whether a fault or transient\n              reason keeps them is the analog reviewer's call. The\n              positions are kept so neither outcome needs a redraw.\nThe other standing requirement is unchanged: with the board off and the\ninputs energized, 3V3/B5 must stay <=0.3 V against about 2.78 mA of\npresent injection (S3.1). No part is selected and selecting one is not\nthis task: it is the analog reviewer and LRA-02. Isolation after the\ndivider does not qualify; series limiting and firmware high-Z are not\nisolation."
		(at 845.82 68.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b3bccd2d-1406-406e-b803-f0f2e8542830")
	)
	(text "Ignition opto cell"
		(at 845.82 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c77dd74c-0756-4f5d-ac62-98585a39d79e")
	)
	(text "Fitted cell (AS_BUILT S3.4): B11 -> 1N5819 -> measured 2.2k -> LED anode;\nLED cathode returns to B16 with nothing in series; collector to the report\npath, emitter to PGND, fitted 100 nF across the output. No input capacitor.\nDESIGN.md S3 instead returns the LED to PGND and uses 1k/1N4148 - this\ncapture follows the fitted cell, per the packet. Q2 raises the consequence:\nthe fitted return puts 4.7-5.8 mA of LED current in B16, which S4 declares\nreference-only with no current intended.\nRev A does not take the opto collector to GP5 (D-RA-03 forbids mixing the\nold raw-GP5 rule with the qualified proposal). GP5 is QUAL_N_REPORT, drained\nby XQUAL and pulled up by RIGN to switched 3V3. XQUAL has no component-level\ndesign in this task input - Q1."
		(at 845.82 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08e70778-63df-4be4-9d2a-601d5ebbc4f8")
	)
	(text "Pico W pin map"
		(at 845.82 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7239af4a-8c60-41cf-bb51-b8280cf04b99")
	)
	(text "GP0/GP1, GP7, GP8-GP10 and GP28 are deliberately unconnected (X markers).\nGP8-GP10 are offers to LRA-04, not reservations. ARM, EXPIRED, PGOOD and\nHOLD_N stay off the GPIOs: they are A5-domain test points only.\nGP11 and GP12 are brought to pads per S1. ADC_VREF, 3V3_EN and VBUS are\nunconnected as fitted; VBUS has no buck connection (DESIGN.md S3)."
		(at 845.82 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "54e97108-1822-4353-8450-df7f16f4bee4")
	)
	(text "HOLD driver"
		(at 845.82 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd3c8dce-600d-4268-9e6f-53ab66c6dfa5")
	)
	(text "GP6 HOLD_RAW with a 47k external pulldown and the JH maintenance link.\nFirmware latches it LOW before output enable; 4 mA drive, 2.6 V loaded\nqualification target. Open JH for USB maintenance - RBH stays fitted."
		(at 845.82 210.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "33adefbe-8064-496e-865a-15f88218d50e")
	)
	(text "SD"
		(at 845.82 223.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c788600b-eafb-4ed6-9a52-a4aa85bf7b37")
	)
	(text "SPI0 at 12 MHz on switched 3V3 only (GP16 MISO, GP17 CS, GP18 SCK,\nGP19 MOSI). D6 adds bulk at the SD supply: write spikes of 100-200 mA\notherwise land directly on the Pico's shared ~300 mA regulator.\nAny move of this module to a 5 V rail re-opens the MISO clearance gate\nof AS_BUILT S3.5 and must not be done in layout."
		(at 845.82 228.60 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb300852-f4b8-42cd-94f1-56e9ec6ca34c")
	)
	(text "J3 bus and J4 service"
		(at 845.82 246.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2a709c4-fbcb-4485-84e0-ed58ec125f12")
	)
	(text "J3 is unpopulated with every pin unconnected: LRA-04 selected no bus and\nreserved no pin. Do not capture a transceiver here.\nJ4 carries the RUN-to-GND reset pair. Its UART0 pins are present but\nunconnected (Q5). It must be power-off-safe: no externally powered\npull-up into an off GPIO."
		(at 845.82 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6c395b22-7bd3-4356-8b65-62f6b8919cf3")
	)
	(text "Onboard switched power"
		(at 845.82 269.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f1a43c48-5ab1-4adc-b457-34cd93014bc6")
	)
	(text "Reuses the existing 9527a14 power candidate exactly as DESIGN.md S3 lists\nit (D-POWER-02), with two reviewed deltas: D7 onboard switched supply and\nD13 the 1N4004 DOR. Rail nets: P12 always-on, VIN_SW switched, B5 buck\noutput, VSYS through DOR, P3V3_SW from the Pico regulator.\nQP body diode is drain-to-source: it blocks P12 to VIN_SW when off but\ndoes not block reverse energy. For every diode, check the net rather than\nthe footprint - the keyless TVS reversal history makes that essential.\nTVS and XVP are distinct: TVS is a named inherited candidate, XVP is the\nunselected VEHICLE_PROTECTION BOM row. Neither is vehicle-approved.\nBench only: QI and QH are 2N3904 for a 12-16 V bench, and F1 assumes a\ncurrent-limited supply. This is not a vehicle-qualified power stage."
		(at 845.82 274.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bba7465e-d9c2-4538-b43e-7b8e58929270")
	)
	(text "MAX_ON"
		(at 845.82 307.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fa320b21-5f26-4c59-b7e4-3dc11ad76ae9")
	)
	(text "Independent maximum-on timer plus latched HOLD-path inhibit: 32-40 min\nafter IGN fall, non-retriggerable by HOLD, <=40 uA room allocation.\nNot designed and not in stock record; required before unattended use.\nIts A5 and VCLK rails and its ARM/EXPIRED/PGOOD/HOLD_N status nodes are\ncaptured so layout cannot lose them. A5 also supplies XQUAL. HOLD_N is\nNOT inserted into the HOLD path by this capture - Q6."
		(at 845.82 312.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ce3b0e30-1c25-48a6-b695-c6f1e3d548a5")
	)
	(text "Test points and reset"
		(at 845.82 332.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "df9d7a48-9863-4703-ba8a-aea89e5bd9ba")
	)
	(text "Test loops per S5.3, plus TP_GATE and TP_SW from the power BOM TP row.\nThree separate ground loops, following the keyless pattern: buck, Pico and\nharness end. JR shorts RUN to GND for a reset without cutting power.\nCurrent-sensitive nodes must be measurable without the instrument supplying\nthe current being measured, and probes must be removable for the final\nleakage reading - a layout requirement (LRA-08), not only a procedure."
		(at 845.82 337.82 0)
